 are that he's  the only one who can beat Donald Trump  that's why we got to put all our faith  and  policy will come later don't worry about  that in fact about a week ago Biden also  told us he didn't have time to explain  his health care policy  I got a move on I got to worry about  beating Donald Trump you cannot and I  can't stress this enough you can't beat  Donald Trump if you're not out there  offering policies because I know it's  easy to get swept up in the big crowds  at these you know campaign events the  people cheering on these talking points  about beating Donald Trump you see it on  Twitter we've got to beat Trump that's  not the whole country though folks  that's not the average person going  about their lives in their homes because  believe it or not a lot of people in  this country have not been adversely  affected by Donald Trump's policies  they're not benefiting in any way from  them don't get me wrong but they haven't  exactly affected their day to day lives  you know their paychecks haven't  increased but they haven't decreased so  why would I jump ship things are okay  for me personally why would I want to  change this why would I want to risk it  and that's what Democrats have to do a  better job of explaining and and by  Democrats I mean all I don't know  eighty-five who are running for  president we've got plenty who are  explaining Sanders Warren Harris yang  these people are out there Tulsi Gabbard  again they're out there telling us like  this is what I want to do and this is  how it's going to affect you and again  nobody's doing that better than  Elizabeth Warren which is why her poll  numbers are finally starting to tick up  there a little bit but listen I'm not  advocating for one candidate or the  other at this point and I'm not trying  to discourage voting for anyone except  maybe Biden at this point because we're  still in the primaries and I can do that  without worrying if you like Biden fine  but why and be expected to answer that  question what is Biden offering that is  going to make your life better and don't  just say he's gonna beat Trump  that's a cop-out that is a very weak  answer with no substance behind it  because there's really not much evidence  to suggest that Biden will beat Trump oh  you want to look at the polling data the  same polling data that said that Hillary  Clinton was gonna run away with this  thing in 2016  be my guest but if you're putting all  your faith in that then be expected you  know you can go ahead and expect the  same kind of disappointment you had in  2016 what we need to be talking about  what every candidate needs to be talking  about is hard policy not just ideas  either you've got to have again I'm  going to use Elizabeth Warren as the  example because she has done it better  than anybody else you have to have the  roadmap you have to explain how we get  from A to B to C to D to the end goal  all the way every step of the process  you have to be prepared for the  Republican obstruction and you have to  understand and have a plan to counter  that because Republicans aren't going to  let these big ideas go through the green  New Deal the Medicare for all the $15  living wage ain't gonna happen  under the Republicans watch so you  better have a workaround unless of  course you are hundred percent certain  the Democrats are going to retain the  house and take back the Senate in 2020  it's all possible by the way there are  far more Republicans up for re-election  than there are Democrats in the Senate  we could do this we absolutely could do  this but not if you're just out there  saying vote for me because I'm not Trump  we tried that in 2016 and it failed what  did Trump do that was different  well we know who his base is and we know  why they supported him they they like  white people and nobody else we get that  part but there are plenty of Trump  voters who believe it or not not racist  average normal working-class folks and  he was talking policy he was talking  ideas bad ideas and bad policies that he  had no intention of following through on  but he talked about it folks and I think  people miss that in these conversations  and I think most of the Democrats who  are running for president understand  that they don't need this lecture they  don't need to hear me tell them to talk  about policy because they are you can go  to their websites and find every  possible issue under the Sun and find  out what they want to do and how they're  gonna do it but then there's Biden Biden  wants to come out be the happy feel-good  candidate be that maybe a little too  touchy-feely candidate but he wants you  to vote for him because he's not Donald  Trump and I'll be a hundred percent  right now I'm in Florida  a swing state I don't have the luxury of  a protest vote if Biden ends up securing  the Democratic nomination I'm a vote  from a / Biden I'm gonna I'm gonna hold  him accountable if he does something bad  I'm going to report on it but if that's  my only option I'll vote for Biden I'm  not gonna stay home I'm not gonna write  in somebody who doesn't have a chance  because again I'm in a swing state very  tough swing state - but until we get to  that point where a single person has  sealed the deal on who the Democratic  nominee is gonna be I'm gonna hold them  all accountable when Bernie sander  screws up I'm gonna call him out when  Elizabeth Warren does I'm gonna call her  same thing with Harrison Booker and boot  edge edge and I have and I do and I will  because that's our job it should not be  the job of any pundit YouTuber  progressive host it shouldn't be  anybody's job to just promote a single  candidate promote the issues and find  the candidate that fits those the best  yeah we've got some great people running  for president and I do have actually two  people in my head that right now I don't  know which one of them I'm gonna vote  for I love them both I think they're  both great and I think either one o